{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>There shall be no miscarrying womb and no barren woman.</b> So that you may be able to teach your children." "<b>I will fill the number of your days.</b> That you shall live the full measure, as with the oil in the lamp of Elohim — that is, the radical moisture innate to generation. The opposite occurs for the majority of people: a person dies before the radical moisture is exhausted, due to illnesses arising either from defective choice or from the constitution and the elements. And so, when a person's days are fulfilled, he will for the most part see sons to his sons and be able to teach them, as it says: וְהוֹדַעְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ וְלִבְנֵי בָנֶיךָ (Deuteronomy 4:9). And through the long lives of elders, the affairs of the generations are set right, as Scripture recounts happened with Levi, Kehat, and Amram."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "Reading לֵוִי, קְהָת וְעַמְרָם as Levi, Kehat, and Amram — three consecutive generations of Levite patriarchs whose overlapping lifespans bridged the Egyptian bondage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:02.661380458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}